Certainly! Below is a simple Rust program that counts from 1 to 10:

```rust
fn main() {
    for i in 1..=10 {
        println!("{}", i);
    }
}
```

This code uses a `for` loop to iterate over a range from 1 to 10 (inclusive) and prints each number. The `1..=10` syntax creates an inclusive range, meaning it includes both the start and end values.
